WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
A new app counts its
monthly users, in thousands.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.500
Five months, five points,
climbing faster and faster.

3
00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.360
One analyst draws a
straight line through them.

4
00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.550
Looks reasonable.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:15.220
Another draws an exponential curve.

6
00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.940
That looks reasonable too.

7
00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:18.660
So which model is better?

8
00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.350
And can you prove it, or is
it just a matter of taste?

9
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.550
In this mission, you'll
start with the data itself:

10
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.190
unbiased, precise questions
and the relevant variables,

11
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.680
before any model means anything.

12
00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:35.120
Then you'll measure the gap
between each point and a model:

13
00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:38.200
a residual, observed minus predicted.

14
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.630
And you'll square the
residuals and add them up,

15
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.130
to measure how well a model fits.

16
00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.120
Your mission: decide
which model is better,

17
00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.650
and how you could prove it.
